  "term": "guardianship",
  "definition": "In this historical legal-psychology usage, guardianship refers to placing an alleged lunatic under another person’s legal care or control. The source indicates that being put under guardianship did not automatically remove the person’s capacity for every other legal act, such as making a will or being responsible for a wrongful act.",
